# What must NOT reach the build context.
#
# The build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything listed here is the difference
# between a 5 MB context and a 500 MB one. Two entries are load-bearing rather
# than tidy: ml/data holds the exported feature CSV, which is around 100 MB
# after `make export-features`, and frontend/node_modules is larger still.
# Neither is used by the Go build, and shipping them makes every one of the
# nine service builds slower for no reason.

# Research data and reports: regenerable, large, and not read by any service.
ml/data/
ml/reports/
ml/.venv/
ml/**/__pycache__/
ml/**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# NOT ignored: ml/artifacts. The trained model travels in the image, because a
# pod has no host to bind-mount it from.

# The dashboard is built and served separately.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/

# Local build output and runtime state.
bin/
dist/
quantos
*.test
*.out
coverage.html
data/
wal/
*.log

# Infrastructure and docs: not inputs to a Go build, and terraform state in
# particular has no business inside an image layer.
infra/
docs/
deploy/grafana/
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# VCS and editors.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
